class:: Lx
summary:: Multi-Track Sample Looper
categories:: Live Coding, Loops
related:: Classes/Px, Classes/Fx, Classes/Dx

description::
Lx extends link::Classes/Px:: to provide multi-track sample looping. Each subfolder in a given path becomes a loop channel, playing tempo-synced audio through the Px pattern system. Loops integrate with Fx effects, quantization, and the Ndef mixer automatically.

subsection:: Setup

code::
// Boot server and load SynthDefs
Px.loadSynthDefs;

// Load samples — each subfolder becomes a channel
Lx.loadSamples("~/path/to/loop/folders/");
::

subsection:: Basic Usage

code::
// Play all channels
Lx.play;

// Play a single channel
Lx.play(0);

// Stop a channel
Lx.stop(0);

// Stop all
Lx.stop;
::

ClassMethods::

subsection:: Sample Loading

method:: loadSamples
Scans a directory for subfolders. Each subfolder becomes a loop channel. All .wav and .aiff files in each subfolder become the sample pool for that channel.

argument:: path
Path to the parent directory containing subfolders of audio files.

code::
Lx.loadSamples("~/Music/loops/");
::

subsection:: Playback Control

method:: play
Plays one channel or all channels. Creates Px loop patterns internally.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based). If omitted, plays all channels.

argument:: fadeTime
Optional fade-in duration in beats.

code::
Lx.play;        // All channels
Lx.play(0);     // Single channel
Lx.play(0, 16); // Fade in over 16 beats
::

method:: stop
Stops one channel or all channels.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based). If omitted, stops all Lx patterns.

code::
Lx.stop;     // Stop all
Lx.stop(0);  // Stop channel 0
::

subsection:: Parameter Control

method:: amp
Sets the amplitude for a channel.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Amplitude value (0-1). Default: 0.3.

code::
Lx.amp(0, 0.8);
::

method:: buf
Switches to a specific sample in a channel's pool.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: index
Sample index within the channel's buffer pool.

code::
Lx.buf(0, 2);  // Switch channel 0 to sample 2
::

method:: dur
Sets the duration (in beats) for a channel.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Duration in beats. Default: 4.

code::
Lx.dur(0, 8);
::

method:: next
Advances to the next sample in a channel's pool (wraps around).

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

code::
Lx.next(0);
::

method:: prev
Goes to the previous sample in a channel's pool (wraps around).

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

code::
Lx.prev(0);
::

method:: rate
Sets the playback rate for a channel.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Rate value. 1 = normal, 0.5 = half speed, 2 = double speed. Default: 1.

code::
Lx.rate(0, 0.5);
::

method:: start
Sets the start position within the sample.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Start position (0-1). Default: 0.

code::
Lx.start(0, 0.25);  // Start at 25%
::

method:: vol
Sets amplitude for all playing channels.

argument:: value
Amplitude value (0-1).

code::
Lx.vol(0.5);
::

subsection:: Granular Synthesis

method:: grain
Toggles granular synthesis mode for a channel. In grain mode, the sample is played through a cloud of tiny overlapping grains (GrainBuf) instead of a continuous loop (PlayBuf). Calling again toggles back to loop mode.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

code::
Lx.grain(0);  // Switch to grain mode
Lx.grain(0);  // Switch back to loop mode
::

method:: density
Sets the grain density (grains per second). Higher values produce smoother, denser textures. Lower values produce sparse, rhythmic grains.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Grains per second. Default: 10. Range: 1-50+.

code::
Lx.density(0, 30);  // Dense, smooth texture
Lx.density(0, 4);   // Sparse, rhythmic grains
::

method:: grainDur
Sets the duration of each grain in seconds. Smaller grains create clicky, glitchy textures. Larger grains create smooth, overlapping sounds.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Grain duration in seconds. Default: 0.1.

code::
Lx.grainDur(0, 0.01);  // Micro grains, glitchy
Lx.grainDur(0, 0.3);   // Large grains, smooth
::

method:: scatter
Sets position randomness. At 0, grains scan linearly through the buffer. Higher values add random position jitter, making each grain come from a slightly different position.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Scatter amount (0-1). Default: 0.

code::
Lx.scatter(0, 0.3);  // Organic variation
::

method:: spread
Sets pitch variation between grains. Small values add chorus-like warmth. Larger values create abstract, detuned textures.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Pitch spread amount (0-1). Default: 0.

code::
Lx.spread(0, 0.02);  // Subtle chorus/shimmer
Lx.spread(0, 0.2);   // Abstract detuning
::

method:: freeze
Stops position scanning. All grains play from the current position, creating a sustained frozen texture.

argument:: channel
Channel index (0-based).

argument:: value
Freeze state (0 or 1). Default: 0.

code::
Lx.freeze(0, 1);  // Freeze at current position
Lx.freeze(0, 0);  // Resume scanning
::

subsection:: GUI

method:: gui
Opens a GUI window with per-channel controls: sample navigation, amplitude, rate, start position, duration knobs, and mute buttons.

code::
Lx.gui;
::

subsection:: State

method:: bufs
Returns the Dictionary of loaded buffers (channel index to Array of Buffers).

method:: channelCount
Returns the number of loaded channels.

method:: channelNames
Returns an Array of subfolder names (one per channel).

method:: modes
Returns an Array of current mode per channel (\loop or \grain).

method:: tracks
Returns an Array of current sample indices per channel.

examples::

code::
// Setup
Px.loadSynthDefs;
Lx.loadSamples("~/Music/loops/");

// Play all loops
Lx.play;

// Adjust parameters
Lx.amp(0, 0.8);
Lx.rate(1, 0.5);
Lx.start(0, 0.25);
Lx.dur(2, 8);

// Navigate samples
Lx.next(0);
Lx.prev(1);

// Add effects via Fx
Fx(\lx0).reverb(0.3);
Fx(\lx1).delay(0.2);

// Open GUI
Lx.gui;

// Fade in
Lx.play(0, 16);

// Granular synthesis mode
Lx.grain(0);
Lx.density(0, 30);
Lx.grainDur(0, 0.2);
Lx.scatter(0, 0.3);
Lx.spread(0, 0.02);

// Frozen texture
Lx.freeze(0, 1);
Lx.freeze(0, 0);

// Granular via Number DSL
1.grain("fm-2:4").dur(4).density(20).scatter(0.3).spread(0.02);

// Stop
Lx.stop;
::
